{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788354121428,"sessionID":"ses_f9dc9f3b3ffeE1zR14fpXVoItC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_81278eda1d1443dfab6d83ed","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/staged_20260902_160140_swi_glu/task.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/staged_20260902_160140_swi_glu/task.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # SwiGLU CANNBench review task\n2: \n3: Review the existing generated `candidate.py`; do not redesign it unless a\n4: concrete defect is found. The exact public schema is:\n5: \n6: `swi_glu(input: Tensor, dim: int = -1) -> Tensor`\n7: \n8: Split the even-sized selected dimension into `x0`, `x1` and compute in f32:\n9: `(x0 * sigmoid(x0)) * x1`; cast once to the input dtype. Output shape equals\n10: input shape with the selected dimension halved. Numerical work must remain in\n11: `@asc2.jit`; torch is limited to allocation, contiguity and metadata views.\n12: \n13: The 20 official routes cover f16/f32/bf16, rank 2 through 5, dimensions\n14: `-1/0/1/2`, aligned and prime tails, 150K through 134M input elements, ranges\n15: from tiny values through f16 boundaries and ±1000, plus zero, Inf and NaN.\n16: Critical routes are `[363,367,14]` bf16 dim=-1; `[1000003,2]` bf16 dim=1;\n17: `[11,13,16,67]` f32 NaN dim=2; and row-axis splits where contiguous halves\n18: cannot be assumed. The pinned v2 2-D copy path requires the final copied\n19: dimension to be at least 32 bytes; a separate 1-D metadata-split path may be\n20: used for narrower layouts.\n21: \n22: The existing seed already passes all 20 exact-v2 dispatch/lowering routes.\n23: Preserve that status. Local compilation proves neither numerical correctness\n24: nor NPU performance. Run only `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` and finish\n25: with `REVIEW_DONE`.\n\n(End of file - total 25 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# SwiGLU CANNBench review task\n\nReview the existing generated `candidate.py`; do not redesign it unless a\nconcrete defect is found. The exact public schema is:\n\n`swi_glu(input: Tensor, dim: int = -1) -> Tensor`\n\nSplit the even-sized selected dimension into `x0`, `x1` and compute in f32:\n`(x0 * sigmoid(x0)) * x1`; cast once to the input dtype. Output shape equals\ninput shape with the selected dimension halved. Numerical work must remain in\n`@asc2.jit`; torch is limited to allocation, contiguity and metadata views.\n\nThe 20 official routes cover f16/f32/bf16, rank 2 through 5, dimensions\n`-1/0/1/2`, aligned and prime tails, 150K through 134M input elements, ranges\nfrom tiny values through f16 boundaries and ±1000, plus zero, Inf and NaN.\nCritical routes are `[363,367,14]` bf16 dim=-1; `[1000003,2]` bf16 dim=1;\n`[11,13,16,67]` f32 NaN dim=2; and row-axis splits where contiguous halves\ncannot be assumed. The pinned v2 2-D copy path requires the final copied\ndimension to be at least 32 bytes; a separate 1-D metadata-split path may be\nused for narrower layouts.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/staged_20260902_160140_swi_glu/task.md","text":"# SwiGLU CANNBench review task\n\nReview the existing generated `candidate.py`; do not redesign it unless a\nconcrete defect is found. The exact public schema is:\n\n`swi_glu(input: Tensor, dim: int = -1) -> Tensor`\n\nSplit the even-sized selected dimension into `x0`, `x1` and compute in f32:\n`(x0 * sigmoid(x0)) * x1`; cast once to the input dtype. Output shape equals\ninput shape with the selected dimension halved. Numerical work must remain in\n`@asc2.jit`; torch is limited to allocation, contiguity and metadata views.\n\nThe 20 official routes cover f16/f32/bf16, rank 2 through 5, dimensions\n`-1/0/1/2`, aligned and prime tails, 150K through 134M input elements, ranges\nfrom tiny values through f16 boundaries and ±1000, plus zero, Inf and NaN.\nCritical routes are `[363,367,14]` bf16 dim=-1; `[1000003,2]` bf16 dim=1;\n`[11,13,16,67]` f32 NaN dim=2; and row-axis splits where contiguous halves\ncannot be assumed. The pinned v2 2-D copy path requires the final copied\ndimension to be at least 32 bytes; a separate 1-D metadata-split path may be\nused for narrower layouts.\n\nThe existing seed already passes all 20 exact-v2 dispatch/lowering routes.\nPreserve that status. Local compilation proves neither numerical correctness\nnor NPU performance. Run only `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` and finish\nwith `REVIEW_DONE`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":25,"totalLines":25,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/staged_20260902_160140_swi_glu/task.md","time":{"start":1788354121423,"end":1788354121427}},"id":"prt_062364d5c001qyjM9n5VcuiKgn","sessionID":"ses_f9dc9f3b3ffeE1zR14fpXVoItC","messageID":"msg_06236462d001KVgrV5xdW1gVQ2"}}
