{"type":"text","timestamp":1788354200650,"sessionID":"ses_f9dc9f3b3ffeE1zR14fpXVoItC","part":{"id":"prt_062376aa7001KvPfQxYYNYANY8","messageID":"msg_062364eeb0019WjPEvuOiRicHC","sessionID":"ses_f9dc9f3b3ffeE1zR14fpXVoItC","type":"text","text":"I've reviewed the candidate against the contract. Let me verify my analysis:\n\n**Public contract**: `swi_glu(input: Tensor, dim: int = -1) -> Tensor` ✓ (candidate.py:55)\n\n**Host/JIT boundary**: torch used only for `contiguous()`, `narrow()`, `empty()` ✓; all numerical work (`exp`, `div`, multiplies) inside `@asc2.jit` ✓\n\n**Numerical formula**: `sig = 1/(1+exp(-x0f))`, `y = x0f * sig * x1f` in f32, single cast back via `y.to(x0.dtype)` ✓ (matches `(x0 * sigmoid(x0)) * x1`)\n\n**Tails**: 2D path uses `n = half_inner - col_off` with `real_shape=[1, n]` (candidate.py:24-27,32); 1D path uses `n = size - off` with `real_shape=[n]` (candidate.py:45-47,52) ✓\n\n**Dtypes**: f16/f32/bf16 all funneled through `.to(asc.float32)` then back to `x0.dtype` ✓\n\n**Special values**: NaN→NaN, ±Inf and zero follow IEEE-754 formula exactly as specified (no special-casing needed since golden uses same f32 formula) ✓\n\n**UB budget**: per-tile = 1024 elems; worst case f32 = 1024×4B × (x0,x1,x0f,x1f,sig,y) ≈ 24KB « 253952B ✓\n\n**32-byte 2D copy guard**: 2D path taken when `half_inner*esize >= 32` (candidate.py:86); narrower layouts routed to 1D metadata-split path ✓\n\n**Cores**: `min(72, num_tiles)` ≤ 72 ✓\n\n**Dim split correctness**: 2D view `[outer, c_inner]` with `x1_off = half_inner + col_off` correctly addresses second half since `c_inner = 2*half_inner` for even C ✓\n\nNo concrete defect found — the seed correctly preserves the 20-route lowering status. Running the required compile check:","time":{"start":1788354194087,"end":1788354200649}}}
